\
## Frequently asked questions\
\
**Q: My Dice score is only 0.6 \'97 is that bad?**  \
A: It depends on your tissue.  For densely packed cells that are very similar between\
sections, a good score is > 0.85.  For sparse or variable tissue, 0.6\'960.75 may be\
the best achievable.  Check the live preview visually \'97 sometimes the overlay looks\
good even when the score is modest.\
\
**Q: The tool runs for a long time on the B-Spline step.**  \
A: This is normal for large images.  The B-Spline step is the most thorough.  You can\
speed it up by reducing `bspline_config.iters` (e.g. to `100`) at the cost of some precision.\
\
**Q: The overlay preview shows the masks are completely separate.**  \
A: The FFT pre-alignment may have failed.  Try reducing `fft_spacing` (e.g. to `0.5`)\
to make the initial search more precise.\
\
**Q: I get an error about "empty mask".**  \
A: The tool could not find any foreground pixels in one of the mask files.  Check that:\
- You entered the correct filename\
- The mask file is not all-black\
- For TIFF files: try setting `tiff_3d_mode=stack_as_channels` if your mask is a Z-stack\
\
**Q: My images are rotated relative to each other by more than ~10\'b0.**  \
A: Switch the *Alignment method* to `rotation`.  This adds a rotational search before\
the SDM/B-Spline stages.\
\
**Q: Can I re-apply the same transform to new channel images?**  \
A: Not directly through the GUI yet.  The composite transform is saved as\
`Coregistration_composite.h5` and can be loaded and applied programmatically\
using SimpleITK.\
\
