\
## Technical details (for developers)\
\
The pipeline lives in `mexalign/core/`.  \
The entry points are:\
\
```bash\
# Graphical interface\
python -m mexalign.gui_full\
\
# Command-line (headless, for batch processing)\
python -m mexalign.cli_full \\\
  --directory /path/to/case \\\
  --script-variant core \\\
  --override fft_spacing=1.5 \\\
  --override coarse_config.iters=150\
```\
\
Module layout:\
\
| File | Responsibility |\
|---|---|\
| `core/config.py` | All algorithm parameters and their defaults |\
| `core/image_io.py` | Reading and writing images (PNG, TIFF, multi-channel) |\
| `core/features.py` | FFT-based translation estimation |\
| `core/logic.py` | Core algorithms (SDM, gradients, erosion, registration runner) |\
| `core/pipeline.py` | Orchestrates all stages; headless (no Qt dependency) |\
| `core/signals.py` | Lightweight signal/slot system (mirrors Qt signals without the Qt dependency) |\
| `gui_full.py` | PySide6 graphical interface |\
| `compat_runner.py` | Connects GUI/CLI inputs to the pipeline; handles multiple variants |\
| `contracts.py` | Data structures for inputs and results |\
| `pipeline.py` | Dice/IoU evaluation |\
| `metrics.py` | Dice and IoU calculation |\
| `io_masks.py` | Binary mask loading for evaluation |\
| `legacy/` | Rotation and gradient-turned variant scripts |\
}